<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  DEMO VERSION 1 — federate Ifremer's global ArgoFloats dataset.

  EDDTableFromErddap is a *redirect* mirror: data requests are handed off to the
  remote ERDDAP, which answers the client directly. Consequences (per the ERDDAP
  datasets.xml docs, https://erddap.github.io/docs/server-admin/datasets):

  - GLOBAL SCOPE ONLY. There is no way to bake in a row filter such as
    data_center="ME" (Canada/MEDS): this type supports no constraints, and no
    ERDDAP dataset type can serve a fixed row-subset of a remote server
    (defaultDataQuery only pre-fills the form; users can clear it). A
    Canadian-only dataset requires owning the files - that is demo version 2
    (ARGO_MEDS.xml + the Argo_MEDS_Parser pipeline).
  - NO METADATA CONTROL. addAttributes / dataVariable sections are forbidden
    for this type; title, summary, and cdm_data_type come from Ifremer as-is.
  - NOT CDE-HARVESTABLE. Ifremer advertises cdm_data_type=TrajectoryProfile,
    which the CIOOS Data Explorer harvester (cde_harvester) skips
    (CDM_DATA_TYPE_UNSUPPORTED). This fragment is a catalogue/federation demo
    and a convenience link to the global dataset on the national server.
  - AVAILABILITY is Ifremer's: their ERDDAP has been observed to be slow or
    time out; requests redirect there, so this dataset is only as fast as they are.
  - Kept in sync via ERDDAP's subscription system (this server subscribes to
    the remote dataset's change notifications automatically).

  Installed into cioos-national-erddap/datasets.d/ by
  GenerateDatasetsXml_argofederated.sh. Deliberately NOT added via
  erddap_servers.yaml - that would harvest Ifremer's entire catalogue and the
  entry would be subject to the sync's stale-harvest cleanup.

  Clients CAN of course apply the Canada filter per-request, e.g.:
    .../tabledap/ArgoFloats_Ifremer.csv?...&data_center=%22ME%22
-->
<erddapDatasets>

    <dataset type="EDDTableFromErddap" datasetID="ArgoFloats_Ifremer" active="true">
        <sourceUrl>https://erddap.ifremer.fr/erddap/tabledap/ArgoFloats</sourceUrl>
    </dataset>

</erddapDatasets>
